  <h3>Example 12: Small Mechanical Bracket</h3>
  <p>A flat right-triangular bracket has a hypotenuse of 250 mm and a perpendicular altitude of 120 mm: <span set:html={rich('[[K=(250\\times120)/2]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{K=15000\\text{ mm}^2}]]]')} /> The answer is in square millimetres because the inputs are in millimetres. Since <span set:html={rich('[[1\\text{ cm}^2=100\\text{ mm}^2]]')} />, this equals <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{150\\text{ cm}^2}]]]')} /> Converting the linear unit and converting the square unit are different operations, as the units section explains.</p>

