        <tr class="border-b border-primary/10"><td class="py-3 pr-4">Area from legs</td><td class="py-3 pr-4"><span set:html={rich('[[a]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b]]')} /></td><td class="py-3">Simplest when the two legs are known</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-primary/10"><td class="py-3 pr-4">Area from altitude</td><td class="py-3 pr-4"><span set:html={rich('[[c]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[h]]')} /></td><td class="py-3">Direct when the hypotenuse and perpendicular altitude are known</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-primary/10"><td class="py-3 pr-4">Area from angle</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Appropriate sides and included angle</td><td class="py-3">Useful when an acute angle is known</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-3 pr-4">Area from inradius</td><td class="py-3 pr-4"><span set:html={rich('[[r]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[s]]')} /></td><td class="py-3">Useful in incircle and semiperimeter problems</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The same right triangle's area does not change when another valid method is used. Pick the row that matches the numbers already in hand; when two rows are available, their agreement is a free correctness check.</p>
</section>

